&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Sword, we’re building AI to heal billions and unlock humanity’s full potential. In doing so, we’re pioneering AI Care, a fundamentally new approach to healthcare built for medical reasoning, safety, and real-time treatment, not generic technology applied after the fact. As both a clinical-centric frontier AI lab and an applied AI platform, Sword is reimagining how care is delivered at scale, removing traditional barriers like appointments, waiting rooms, and stigma so more people can access the care they need—and ultimately get back to lives lived in full.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since 2020, Sword has expanded across physical therapy, women’s health, cardiometabolic, and mental health, and is now moving beyond the session to a fully AI-native, 24/7 care program that brings physical activity, therapeutic exercise, psychotherapy, nutrition, and behavior change into one connected experience. More than 700,000 members across three continents have completed over 10 million AI sessions, helping 1,000+ enterprise clients avoid more than $1 billion in unnecessary healthcare costs. Backed by 42 clinical studies, 44+ patents, and more than $500 million raised from leading investors including Khosla Ventures, General Catalyst, and Founders Fund, Sword is defining a new standard for healthcare.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;AI&amp;nbsp;Proficiency at Sword&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI fluency is a core expectation at Sword. Every candidate is assessed against our three-level framework — be ready to share real examples of how AI is already part of how you work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Explorer (Level 1) — Uses AI daily to boost personal productivity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Builder (Level 2) — Creates workflows and tools that elevate the whole team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Integrator (Level 3) — Embeds AI into products and processes at scale&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every hire must demonstrate at least Level 1. The expected level will vary depending on the seniority of the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sword Health is looking for an exceptional go-getter to join our team as a Lifecycle Marketing Operations Specialist to own the execution and deployment of our data-driven marketing initiatives. This role requires an independent self-starter who can flawlessly deliver the baseline but also proactively seeks to improve existing processes to increase efficiency and scalability. A subject-matter-expert who can manage, build and execute against requirements from various stakeholders. Collaborating intimately across Growth, Data, Product, Engineering, and Marketing teams will be core to success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage day-to-day campaign production, QA, execution, reporting &amp;amp; optimization of marketing campaigns and programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own implementation of automated journeys and blast campaigns from start to finish, across multiple channels including email, sms, push, in-app and direct mail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with various teams, including Enrollment, Growth, Member Engagement, Content, Creative, Data, Product &amp;amp; Engineering to launch communications across Sword-owned channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that Marketing Operations standards are met, including proper naming conventions, event conversion tagging, and QA prior to campaign deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and optimize multiple campaigns &amp;amp; programs at a time, ensuring that campaigns launch and deliver on schedule and according to expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify issues leading up to a launch and during a live campaign that would prevent campaign success, working with key stakeholders to solve and troubleshoot as necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Code logic in email template to personalize content for 1:1 experience using scripting language such as Handlebars, Liquid, AMPScript, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and own improvements on operational processes to improve efficiency and scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uncover hidden opportunities for the improvement of processes and data. Proactively find blockers and challenges to our growth, then take the initiative to solve them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Growth &amp;amp; Engineering teams to ensure data pipelines are set up between marketing systems for real time data updates, event triggers, and member profile updates prior to campaign launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and document best practices approach for gathering and analyzing data to identify key performance indicators, prioritization, and optimization strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 2 year experience in Lifecycle/Marketing Operations with at least one marketing automation platform, such as Iterable, Braze, Salesforce Marketing Cloud, Cordial, Marketo, etc. (Iterable a plus, but not necessary)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in building and deploying omni-channel messaging, including email, push, SMS, in-app, direct mail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge in HTML/CSS with experience in coding mobile-first email templates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of email clients and strengths/limitations of each&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with scripting languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about understanding the member journey at each stage of their lifecycle and building member journey flows to optimize the member experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Action-oriented and deadline-driven, with high level of project management and time management skills to prioritize deadlines and requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced environment with rapidly changing requirements and shifting priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independent, self-starter who can work autonomously and deliver results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An enthusiastic, take-charge attitude, coupled with a desire to collaborate and learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills to set expectations and provide progress with stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Impeccable attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate with multiple teams across multiple time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytically driven, with ability to gather insights across multiple channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;*The range below reflects base, variable, and equity for this role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;This is a starting point, not a ceiling — once someone joins and proves they&#39;re outlier talent, we adjust quickly to make sure their compensation matches their impact.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot; style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Job titles may span more than one career level, so actual pay depends on skills, qualifications, experience, location, and market demand, among other factors. The range reflects base salary plus any variable, bonus, or sales incentives, and our estimate of the value of private company stock options where applicable. It&#39;s subject to change, and future stock value isn&#39;t guaranteed. Sword also offers additional benefits beyond total compensation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Total Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€41.300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€64.900 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;sup&gt;Country-specific benefits may vary and will be detailed separately.&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;sup&gt;Sword Health complies with applicable Federal and State civil rights laws and does not discriminate on the basis of Age, Ancestry, Color, Citizenship, Gender, Gender expression, Gender identity, Gender information, Marital status, Medical condition, National origin, Physical or mental disability, Pregnancy, Race, Religion, Caste, Sexual orientation, and Veteran status.&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
